# Termcap database for the bundled environment, in the classic
# /etc/termcap format BusyBox's termcap reader parses. Entries are
# kept self-contained (no tc= includes) and cover the capabilities
# full-screen programs (vi, top, less) actually use: screen clear,
# cursor addressing, insert/delete line and char, standout and
# underline modes, alternate screen (ti/te via DECSET 1049) and
# cursor visibility. The 256-colour entries add Co/pa/AF/AB.

